{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01DBVmJJoW1swtYcJAwJKGvj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q8: Ingest structured, unstructured, event data?**\n\n---\n\n**`answers/06-008-ingest-structured-unstructured-event-data.md`**\n\nThe answer is organised around a **three-class ingestion framework**:\n\n| Class | Key tools | Sink |\n|-------|-----------|------|\n| **Structured** (DB, CSV, DW) | Debezium CDC → Kafka, Airflow batch | Feast/Tecton feature store, Parquet S3 |\n| **Unstructured** (PDFs, docs, audio) | PyMuPDF, Textract, Whisper, GPT-4o vision | Pinecone/Qdrant (vector) + S3 (raw) |\n| **Events** (Kafka, clickstreams) | Apache Flink windowed aggregations | Redis (online features), BigQuery (offline) |\n\nShared quality gates across all three: **Presidio PII scrubbing**, **Great Expectations schema validation**, **MinHash/idempotency-key dedup**, and Grafana observability.\n\nThe key production heuristic: **choose batch vs stream based on the staleness SLA** — streaming (Kafka+Flink) adds real operational complexity (exactly-once checkpointing, watermarking) that's only justified when you need <1s freshness. For a nightly document re-index, batch wins.\n\n19 plan items remaining in `06-ml-fundamentals`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":69765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":375,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f41ad2ac-76f0-4150-a29c-bc1ac719dd2a","uuid":"1a280c78-a8bb-4a39-8393-149d9a9b7313"}
